## Model Fallback

When a model is unavailable, Cursor falls back to the next available model:

- `composer-2-fast` model agents (explore, librarian) — always available
- If a worker fails with a model error, retry with `model: "composer-2-fast"`
- After 2 model failures on the same agent type, switch to a different agent type

**Retry guidance chain** (mirrors `delegate-task-retry` hook injected into context after Task failures):

1. **Rate limit** — Wait ~30s, retry; if it keeps happening, use `model: "composer-2-fast"`.
2. **Model unavailable** — Retry with `model: "composer-2-fast"`; if the worker was `sisyphus`, consider `sisyphus-junior` as a lighter fallback.
3. **Timeout** — Split the work into smaller subtasks or delegate with a simpler `subagent_type`.
4. **Other errors** — Resume the same subagent ID with concrete fix context; after **more than 3** failures for the same agent type, treat as escalation: try another agent type, prefer `model: "composer-2-fast"`, or ask the user.

| Agent | Primary Model | Fallback |
|-------|--------------|----------|
| explore | composer-2-fast | Always available |
| librarian | composer-2-fast | Always available |
| sisyphus-junior | composer-2-fast | Retry with composer-2-fast |
| sisyphus | claude-opus-4-7-thinking-high | Retry with sisyphus-junior |
| hephaestus | gpt-5.3-codex-high-fast | Retry with sisyphus |
| oracle | gpt-5.4-medium | Retry with composer-2-fast |

## Hard Constraints

| NEVER (any mode) | NEVER (any mode) |
|-------------------|-------------------|
| Commit without user request | Speculate about unread code |
| Type suppression (as any, @ts-ignore) | Empty catch blocks |
| Deleting failing tests | Shotgun debugging |

**Mode-specific constraints** (FORBIDDEN lists per mode) are in `orchestrator-reference.mdc`. Obey the FORBIDDEN list for the active mode.

